1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:04,217
Time doesn't need to be managed.
Your priorities need to be managed.

2
00:00:04,457 --> 00:00:07,967
We have the cookie-cutter
information

3
00:00:08,027 --> 00:00:09,907
about how to manage your calendars

4
00:00:10,257 --> 00:00:13,027
and how to spend X amount of time
on certain things.

5
00:00:13,037 --> 00:00:17,895
Now we're moving from managing time
to managing what's important.

6
00:00:18,055 --> 00:00:20,695
And I wanna say something
that a lot of people won't say:

7
00:00:20,830 --> 00:00:25,442
But at some point, you're gonna have to
choose what your priorities are.

8
00:00:25,578 --> 00:00:28,568
I know we like to say we have
competing priorities.

9
00:00:28,653 --> 00:00:30,683
At some point,
something has to win.

10
00:00:30,798 --> 00:00:33,298
You have to choose one thing
over the other.

11
00:00:33,435 --> 00:00:35,605
If you wanna actually be effective.
